frame·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀Ê␀␀␀␀␀␀␀,m_ManagerSingletonMode·„␀␀Ê␀␀␀␀␀␀␀2m_ManagerRegistrationMode·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄˆThe Input System Action that will be used to read Move data from the left hand controller. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¯The Input System Action that will be used to read Move data from the right hand controller. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄˆThe Input System Action that will be used to read Turn data from the left hand controller. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¯The Input System Action that will be used to read Turn data from the right hand controller. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å␀The Input System Action that will be used to read Snap Turn data from the left hand controller. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action that will be used to read Snap Turn data from the right hand controller. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀XThe Locomotion Provider object to listen to.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä†The minimum height of the character's capsule that will be set by this behavior.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä†The maximum height of the character's capsule that will be set by this behavior.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀`The speed, in units per second, to move forward.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀pControls whether to enable strafing (sideways movement).·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄºControls whether to enable flying (unconstrained movement). This overrides the use of gravity.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä‘Controls whether gravity affects this provider when a Character Controller is used and flying is disabled.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀XControls when gravity begins to take effect.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀jThe source Transform to define the forward direction.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄêThe number of degrees/second clockwise to rotate when turning clockwise.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä†The 2D Input Axis on the controller devices that will be used to trigger a move.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅA list of controllers that allow move.  If an XRController is not enabled, or does not have input actions enabled, move will not work.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÙValue below which input values will be clamped. After clamping, values will be renormalized to [0, 1] between min and max.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÙValue above which input values will be clamped. After clamping, values will be renormalized to [0, 1] between min and max.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä†The 2D Input Axis on the controller devices that will be used to trigger a turn.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅA list of controllers that allow Turn.  If an XRController is not enabled, or does not have input actions enabled, turn will not work.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÙValue below which input values will be clamped. After clamping, values will be renormalized to [0, 1] between min and max.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÙValue above which input values will be clamped. After clamping, values will be renormalized to [0, 1] between min and max.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä™The 2D Input Axis on the controller devices that will be used to trigger a snap turn.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å A list of controllers that allow Snap Turn.  If an XRController is not enabled, or does not have input actions enabled, snap turn will not work.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÆThe deadzone that the controller movement will have to be above to trigger a snap turn.	␀␀␀␀Ä⁄LocomotionPhase.Idle is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. Use LocomotionState.Idle instead.␀	␀␀␀␀ÄÍLocomotionPhase.Started is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. Use LocomotionState.Preparing instead.␀	␀␀␀␀Ä‚LocomotionPhase.Moving is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. Use LocomotionState.Moving instead.␀	␀␀␀␀Ä‹LocomotionPhase.Done is deprecated and will be removed in a future release. Use LocomotionState.Ended instead.␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀~The timeout (in seconds) for exclusive access to the XR Origin.·„␀␀Ê␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀m_XRRig␀␀dThe XR Origin object to provide access control to.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄåThe number of degrees clockwise to rotate when snap turning clockwise.·„␀␀