his Input Module.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅÇWhen enabled, additional sorting is run to ensure things closer to the point of interaction are considered first. It is recommended to enable this for XR devices and disable for non-XR devices.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀"‚␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀Input Devices␀␀␀␀␀xIf true, will forward 3D tracked device data to UI elements.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÃIf true, will forward 2D mouse data to UI elements. Ignored when any Input System UI Actions are used.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÃIf true, will forward 2D touch data to UI elements. Ignored when any Input System UI Actions are used.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä If true, will forward gamepad data to UI elements. Ignored when any Input System UI Actions are used.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÃIf true, will forward joystick data to UI elements. Ignored when any Input System UI Actions are used.©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀.Input System UI Actions␀␀␀␀␀ÄúPointer input action reference, such as a mouse or single-finger touch device.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄêLeft-click input action reference, typically the left button on a mouse.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄòMiddle-click input action reference, typically the middle button on a mouse.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄîRight-click input action reference, typically the right button on a mouse.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄñScroll wheel input action reference, typically the scroll wheel on a mouse.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å2Navigation input action reference will change which UI element is currently selected to the one up, down, left of or right of the currently selected one.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä“Submit input action reference will trigger a submission of the currently selected UI in the Event System.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä‘Cancel input action reference will trigger canceling out of the currently selected UI in the Event System.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä»When enabled, built-in Input System actions will be used if no Input System UI Actions are assigned."‚␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¿Name of the horizontal axis for gamepad/joystick UI navigation when using the old Input Manager."‚␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄºName of the vertical axis for gamepad/joystick UI navigation when using the old Input Manager."‚␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä÷Name of the gamepad/joystick button to use for UI selection or submission when using the old Input Manager."‚␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä÷Name of the gamepad/joystick button to use for UI cancel or back commands when using the old Input Manager.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀©·␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀8Local Space Anchor Transform␀␀^Local space anchor position for the right hand.¶·␀␀␀␀\Local space anchor position for the left hand.¶·␀␀␀␀^Local space anchor rotation for the right hand.¶·␀␀␀␀\Local space anchor rotation for the left hand.©·␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀.Show Menu Configuration␀␀Ä“Reference axis equivalent used for comparisons with the user's gaze direction and the world up direction.¶·␀␀␀␀Å
Given that the default reference hand for menus is the left hand, it may be required to mirror the reference axis for the right hand.¶·␀␀␀␀ÄÜWhether or not check if the palm reference axis is facing the user.¶·␀␀␀␀Ä¨The angle threshold in degrees to check if the palm reference axis is facing the user.¶·␀␀␀␀zWhether or not check if the palm reference axis is facing up.¶·␀␀␀␀Ä†The angle threshold in degrees to check if the palm reference axis is facing up.©·␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀.Hide Menu Configuration␀␀Ä‹The amount of time in seconds to wait before hiding the following element after the hand is no longer tracked.¶·␀␀␀␀ÄﬁThe additional threshold angle, in degrees, used as a buffer to hide the menu when the palm is facing the user.¶·␀␀␀␀Ä“The additional threshold angle, in degrees, used as a buffer to hide the menu when the palm is facing up.©·␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀4Snap-To-Gaze Configuration␀␀xWhether to snap the following element to the gaze direction.¶·␀␀␀␀Ä¶The angle threshold in degrees to snap the following element to the gaze direction.©·␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀.Smoothing Configuration␀␀ÄîWhether to allow smoothing of the following element position and rotation.¶·␀␀␀␀LThe lower bound of smoothing to apply.¶·␀␀␀␀LThe upper bound of smoothing to apply.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä∏Child GameObject used to hold the hand menu UI. This is the transform that moves each frame.©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀Hand alignment␀␀␀␀␀Å
Which hand should the menu anchor to. None will disable the hand menu. Either will try to follow the first hand to meet requirements.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä®Determines the up direction of the menu when the hand menu is looking at the camera.©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀Palm anchor␀␀␀␀␀nAnchor associated with the left palm pose for the hand.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀pAnchor associated with the right palm pose for the hand.©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀.Position follow config.␀␀␀␀␀ÄÇMinimum distance in meters from target before which tween starts.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä∏Maximum distance in meters from target before tween targets, when time threshold is reached.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄºTime required to elapse before the max distance allowed goes from the min distance to the max.©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀*Gaze Alignment Config␀␀␀␀␀ÅRIf true, menu will hide when gaze to menu origin's divergence angle is above the threshold. In other words, the menu will only show if looking roughly in it's direction.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄöOnly show menu if gaze to menu origin's divergence angle is below this value.¶·␀␀·„␀␀␀␀Å␀An angle, in degrees, that is subtracted from the gaze divergence angle to create the threshold used to trigger hiding the menu.␀␀␀©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀$Animation Settings␀␀␀␀␀lShould the menu animate when it is revealed or hidden.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀bDuration of the reveal/hide animation in seconds.©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀$Selection Behavior␀␀␀␀␀ÄºShould the menu hide when a selection is made with the hand for which the menu is anchored to.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÍXR Interaction Manager used to determine if a hand is selecting. Will find one if None. Used for Hide Menu On Select.©·␀␀·„␀␀␀␀Follow presets␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅéThe behavior that this provider communicates with for access to the mediator's XR Body Transformer. If one is not provided, this provider will attempt to locate one during its Awake or OnEnable call.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe queue order of this provider's transformations of the XR Origin. The lower the va