e amount of time, in seconds, for which the user must hover over the volume before it designates a destination anchor.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅÜWhether to periodically query the filter for its calculated destination. If the determined anchor is not the current destination, the volume will initiate re-evaluation of the destination anchor.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä»The amount of time, in seconds, between queries to the filter for its calculated destination anchor.·„␀␀4f␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇ¿␀·Æ␀␀Å2The anchor filter used to evaluate a teleportation destination. If set to None, the volume will use the anchor furthest from the user as the destination.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀xThe Transform that represents the teleportation destination.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄåThe transforms that represent the possible teleportation destinations.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀xSettings for how this volume evaluates a destination anchor.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄåThe time (in seconds) to delay the teleportation once it is activated.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÜControls whether to enable unconstrained movement along the x-axis.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÜControls whether to enable unconstrained movement along the y-axis.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÜControls whether to enable unconstrained movement along the z-axis.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀XControls when gravity begins to take effect.␀␀Äƒm_GravityApplicationMode has been deprecated in XRI 3.0.0 and will be removed in a future version.·„␀␀¶·␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å4Controls whether gravity applies to constrained axes when a Character Controller is used. Ignored when a Gravity Provider component is found in the scene.␀␀Ä‚Controlling gravity directly in the move provider has been deprecated in XRI 3.1.0, use Gravity Provider instead.	␀␀␀␀Ä‚Controlling gravity directly in the move provider has been deprecated in XRI 3.1.0, use Gravity Provider instead.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀`The speed, in units per second, to move forward.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄŒDetermines how much control the player has while falling in the air (0 = no control, 1 = full control).·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀pControls whether to enable strafing (sideways movement).·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄºControls whether to enable flying (unconstrained movement). This overrides the use of gravity.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀jThe source Transform to define the forward direction.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä»Reads input data from the left hand controller. Input Action must be a Value action type (Vector 2).·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä Reads input data from the right hand controller. Input Action must be a Value action type (Vector 2).·„␀␀¶·␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅƒControls whether gravity affects this provider when a Character Controller is used and flying is disabled. Ignored when a Gravity Provider component is found in the scene. Deprecated in XRI 3.1.0, use Gravity Provider instead.␀␀Ä‚Controlling gravity directly in the move provider has been deprecated in XRI 3.1.0, use Gravity Provider instead.·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Äƒm_GrabMoveAction has been deprecated. Please configure input action using m_GrabMoveInput instead.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä≤The left hand grab move instance which will be used as one half of two-handed locomotion.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¥The right hand grab move instance which will be used as one half of two-handed locomotion.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÙControls whether to override the settings for individual handed providers with this provider's settings on initialization.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄåThe ratio of actual movement distance to controller movement distance.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄíControls whether translation requires both grab move inputs to be active.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀hControls whether to enable yaw rotation of the user.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀nControls whether to enable uniform scaling of the user.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀>The minimum user scale allowed.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀>The maximum user scale allowed.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄêDisable gravity during the jump. This will result in a more floaty jump.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀XAllow player to jump without being grounded.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀jThe number of times a player can jump before landing.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÿThe time window after leaving the ground that a jump can still be performed. Sometimes known as coyote time.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä∂The height (approximately in meters) the player will be when reaching the apex of the jump.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä“Allow the player to stop their jump early when input is released before reaching the maximum jump height.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀jThe minimum amount of time the jump will execute for.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄöThe maximum time a player can hold down the jump button to increase altitude.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä∂The speed at which the jump will decelerate when the player releases the jump button early.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀^Input data that will be used to perform a jump.∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀>Apply gravity to the XR Origin.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀|Apply gravity based on the current Up vector of the XR Origin.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀xDetermines the maximum fall speed based on units per second.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄàDetermines the speed at which a player reaches max gravity velocity.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÃSets the center of the character controller to match the local x and z positions of the player camera.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¢Buffer for the radius of the sphere cast used to check if the player is grounded.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¶Buffer for the distance of the sphere cast used to check if the player is grounded.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄñThe layer mask used for the sphere cast to check if the player is grounded.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å\Whether trigger colliders are considered when using a sphere cast to determine if grounded. Use Global refers to the Queries Hit Triggers setting in Physics Project Settings.¶·␀␀·„␀␀␀␀dEvent that is called when gravity lock is changed.␀␀␀¶·␀␀·„␀␀␀␀`Callback for anytime the grounded state changes.␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀™·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä?·„␀␀™·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä?·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀™·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÕÃLæÕÃL>·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀