␀␀␀␀␀Ä¶The Transform component whose position and rotation will be matched and stabilized.·„␀␀4f␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ˇ¿␀„␀␀Ä‹Optional - When provided a ray, the stabilizer will calculate the rotation that keeps a ray's endpoint stable.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä∆If enabled, will read the target and apply stabilization in local space. Otherwise, in world space.©·␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀0Stabilization Parameters␀␀␀␀␀ÄÇMaximum distance (in degrees) that stabilization will be applied.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÄMaximum distance (in meters) that stabilization will be applied.·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀∞ ␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀Æ·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀PThe unique name for the hand expression.␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀fThe input to trigger the simulated hand expression.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe captured sequence of poses and common gesture data that represent the hand expressionto be simulated when toggled by an input action.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀lThe sequence type whether single-frame or multi-frame.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄòThe singular frame to be played in the case of a single-frame sequence type.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¶The frame used as the starting frame when replaying a multi-frame capture sequence.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¢The frame used as the ending frame when replaying a multi-frame capture sequence.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä÷The frame used as the starting frame when replaying the reverse sequence in a multi-frame capture sequence.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä“The frame used as the ending frame when replaying the reverse sequence in a multi-frame capture sequence.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÍThe list of simulation key frame indices that represent the phases in which the capture sequence will be played back."‚␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄòThe captured hand expression to simulate when the input action is performed.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¢Whether or not this expression appears in the quick action list in the simulator.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀RThe list of hand expressions to simulate.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄñThe resting hand expression to use when no other hand expression is active.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀RThe list of hand expressions to simulate.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄñThe resting hand expression to use when no other hand expression is active.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅInput Action asset containing controls for the simulator itself. Unity will automatically enable and disable it with this component.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä˛Input Action asset containing controls for the simulated controllers. Unity will automatically enable and disable it as needed.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä‹The Input System Action used to translate in the x-axis (left/right) while held. Must be a Value Axis Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä÷The Input System Action used to translate in the y-axis (up/down) while held. Must be a Value Axis Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä‡The Input System Action used to translate in the z-axis (forward/back) while held. Must be a Value Axis Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÍThe Input System Action used to enable manipulation of the left-hand controller while held. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÏThe Input System Action used to enable manipulation of the right-hand controller while held. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¸The Input System Action used to toggle enable manipulation of the left-hand controller when pressed. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä˛The Input System Action used to toggle enable manipulation of the right-hand controller when pressed. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄËThe Input System Action used to toggle enable looking around with the HMD and controllers. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä»The Input System Action used to enable manipulation of the HMD while held. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄƒThe Input System Action used to change between hand and controller mode. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä–The Input System Action used to cycle between the different available devices. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä†The Input System Action used to stop all manipulation. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to translate or rotate by a scaled amount along or about the x- and y-axes. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to translate or rotate by a scaled amount along or about the z-axis. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to cause the manipulated device(s) to rotate when moving the mouse when held. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å<The Input System Action used to toggle between translating or rotating the manipulated device(s) when moving the mouse when pressed. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅlThe Input System Action used to cause the manipulated device(s) to rotate when moving the mouse while held when it would normally translate, and vice-versa. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅÆThe Input System Action used to constrain the translation or rotation to the x-axis when moving the mouse or resetting. May be combined with another axis constraint to constrain to a plane. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅÆThe Input System Action used to constrain the translation or rotation to the y-axis when moving the mouse or resetting. May be combined with another axis constraint to constrain to a plane. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅÆThe Input System Action used to constrain the translation or rotation to the z-axis when moving the mouse or resetting. May be combined with another axis constraint to constrain to a plane. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅNThe Input System Action used to cause the manipulated device(s) to reset position or rotation (depending on the effective manipulation mode). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÓThe Input System Action used to toggle the cursor lock mode for the game window when pressed. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÏThe Input System Action used to toggle enable translation from keyboard inputs when pressed. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to toggle enable manipulation of the Primary2DAxis of the controllers when pressed. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to toggle enable manipulation of the Secondary2DAxis of the controllers when pressed. Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å6The Input System Action used to control the value of one or more 2D Axis controls on the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅXThe Input System Action used to control one or more 2D Axis controls on the opposite hand of the exclusively manipulated controller device. Must be a Value Vector2 Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄˆThe Input System Action used to control the Grip control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¸The Input System Action used to control the Trigger control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to control the PrimaryButton control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to control the SecondaryButton control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄˆThe Input System Action used to control the Menu control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to control the Primary2DAxisClick control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to control the Secondary2DAxisClick control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to control the Primary2DAxisTouch control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to control the Secondary2DAxisTouch control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Input System Action used to control the PrimaryTouch control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å
The Input System Action used to control the SecondaryTouch control of the manipulated controller device(s). Must be a Button Control.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÚInput Action asset containing controls for the simulated hands. Unity will automatically enable and disable it as needed.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å6The Transform that contains the Camera. This is usually the "Head" of XR Origins. Automatically set to the first enabled camera tagged MainCamera if unset.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄÑThe coordinate space in which keyboard translation should operate.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀~The coordinate space in which mouse translation should operate.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¢Speed of translation in the x-axis (left/right) when triggered by keyboard input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄúSpeed of translation in the y-axis (up/down) when triggered by keyboard input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¶Speed of translation in the z-axis (forward/back) when triggered by keyboard input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄûSpeed multiplier applied for body translation when triggered by keyboard input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä®Sensitivity of translation in the x-axis (left/right) when triggered by mouse input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¢Sensitivity of translation in the y-axis (up/down) when triggered by mouse input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä∫Sensitivity of translation in the z-axis (forward/back) when triggered by mouse scroll input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄûSensitivity of rotation along the x-axis (pitch) when triggered by mouse input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄöSensitivity of rotation along the y-axis (yaw) when triggered by mouse input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä™Sensitivity of rotation along the z-axis (roll) when triggered by mouse scroll input.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ç(A boolean value of whether to invert the y-axis of mouse input when rotating by mouse input.
