ger the hand expression.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄòThe captured hand expression to simulate when the input action is performed.·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀␀␀␀·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å6The Transform that contains the Camera. This is usually the "Head" of XR Origins. Automatically set to the first enabled camera tagged MainCamera if unset.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅThe Transform that contains the left controller. Automatically set to the Left Controller reference in the XR Input Modality Manager if unset.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å The Transform that contains the right controller. Automatically set to the Right Controller reference in the XR Input Modality Manager if unset.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅñThe Transform used for left hand aiming. Automatically set to the best fit Aim Pose for the left controller or hand, using the Left Hand Game Object reference from the XR Input Modality Manager if unset.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅúThe Transform used for right hand aiming. Automatically set to the best fit Aim Pose for the right controller or hand, using the Right Hand Game Object reference from the XR Input Modality Manager if unset.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¬The corresponding manager for this simulator that handles the lifecycle of the simulated devices.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¨The corresponding manager for this simulator that handles the simulated hand playback.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä∏The optional Interaction Simulator UI prefab to use along with the XR Interaction Simulator.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä†Whether the HMD should report the pose as fully tracked or unavailable/inferred.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä˙Which tracking values the HMD should report as being valid or meaningful to use, which could mean either tracked or inferred.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä¬Whether the left-hand controller should report the pose as fully tracked or unavailable/inferred.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅWhich tracking values the left-hand controller should report as being valid or meaningful to use, which could mean either tracked or inferred.·„␀␀¶·␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÄƒWhether the right-hand controller should report